<title>TURKEY: Turkish Isbank 9-month profits up.</title>
<headline>Turkish Isbank 9-month profits up.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	1,446.26  vs     803.25</p>
<p>    Net profit			14,462.59  vs   8,032.52</p>
<p>    Net interest income	   48,405.18  vs  20,816.21</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense    20,278.60  vs   8,006.70</p>
<p>    Provisions for bad loans	 737.56  vs     480.88</p>
<p>    Loans			    250,181.26  vs 102,552.62</p>
<p>    Deposits			 382,141.49  vs 197,263.77</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed		  32,616.37  vs  30,355.54</p>
<p>    Equity			    45,485.17  vs  23,641.65</p>
<p>    Capital			   10,000.00  vs  10,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - T.Is Bankasi A.S., one of Turkey's biggest commercial banks.</p>
<p>Figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
